From: "joey.qu" <yal3ay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:26:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] xz1c: snapshot of local ROM work as of 2026-10-08

Local-only commit (not for upload). Backup files (*.bak, *.orig, *.pre*) excluded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I043d47fe5654d47ccf52c648fef732ad22efac2a
---
 fs_mgr/fs_mgr.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs_mgr/fs_mgr.cpp b/fs_mgr/fs_mgr.cpp
index 1d881b95b..22ef5a594 100644
--- a/fs_mgr/fs_mgr.cpp
+++ b/fs_mgr/fs_mgr.cpp
@@ -762,6 +762,22 @@ static int prepare_fs_for_mount(const std::string& blk_device, const FstabEntry&
                 fs_stat |= FS_STAT_UNCLEAN_SHUTDOWN;
             }
 
+            // XZ1C: never run tune2fs on a filesystem that has not been checked. Upgrading
+            // from builds whose fstab still asked for quotas (e.g. 20261005) toggles the
+            // quota feature on first boot; toggling it before e2fsck corrupted /data here
+            // (2026-10-06). So when the quota feature must change, fsck first. Enabling
+            // still gets the usual second fsck below (FS_STAT_QUOTA_ENABLED); unchanged
+            // quotas behave exactly as before.
+            const bool has_quota =
+                    (sb.s_feature_ro_compat & cpu_to_le32(EXT4_FEATURE_RO_COMPAT_QUOTA)) != 0;
+            if (has_quota != entry.fs_mgr_flags.quota) {
+                LINFO << "Checking " << blk_device << " before changing quotas";
+                check_fs(blk_device, entry.fs_type, mount_point, &fs_stat);
+                if (!read_ext4_superblock(blk_device, &sb, &fs_stat)) {
+                    return fs_stat;
+                }
+            }
+
             // Note: quotas should be enabled before running fsck.
             tune_quota(blk_device, entry, &sb, &fs_stat);
         } else {
